{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/995807-insubstantial-or-however-you-say-it","id":995807,"title":"insubstantial or however you say it","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-30T14:34:49-07:00","id":995807,"title":"insubstantial or however you say it","content":"Is there a rote to make yourself unsubstantial to pass through walls and such? I heard there's a rote with forces and life to do that, any help regarding that rote and it's mechanisms is appreciated, thanks in advance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12133-leonardo","name":"Leonardo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T14:53:40-07:00","id":995813,"title":"","content":"There's probably a few ways to do it, but most will include Life for sure. For using only Life, my instinct is Life 4 to alter the physical properties of your body to become intangible. The alterations typically available at Life 3 lead me to believe that it's not the right place for such drastic changes. <br /> <br /> Alternatively, by using Life 3/Spirit 3, you can transform yourself into ephemera. Life 3/Forces 3 can transform yourself into a &quot;force&quot; like fire, electricity, or air. M20's writeup on Forces indicates that it requires Life 5/Forces 3 (which could also be used for the Spirit Effect), but it says &quot;transmute people,&quot; which might mean that you can do it yourself but lack the understanding to do it to other people yet.<br /> <br /> Lastly, you could just use Matter 3 to alter the properties of the wall itself to have a much lower density. This seems to me to be the easiest solution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6384-frozenfishy","name":"Frozenfishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T21:59:46-07:00","id":995958,"title":"","content":"Passing through walls is a feat that the Mage books never really covered, so like Frozenfishy said, it comes down to working out a method. Most of the above could work.<br /> <br /> A Mage with a modernist view of Physics (so basically a Technocrat) could attempt to use Forces 2 to create a shield against the forces that keep atoms from occupying the same space. After all, according to current atomic theory, most of the volume that atoms take up is empty space, with protons and electrons and such creating repellent force against the particles of other atoms. A Mage could alter how they interact with that force, allowing their particles to pass unmolested through the same space nominally occupied by the atoms of walls. Add either Life or Matter as needed, if you care about &quot;locking&quot; Effects (which I don't).<br /> <br /> As a spinoff of the Spirit angle from above, I've sometimes toyed with the idea of a character partially shifting into the Umbra with Spirit 3, for various purposes (like making themselves partially invisible, since they're not wholly there). This might be used to phase through a wall, if the structure in question isn't established enough to have a concrete reflection in the Penumbra. New buildings often aren't reflected in the Umbra, though old and well-used buildings usually do. Whatever the case, the character is essentially shifting themselves out of phase with the wall just enough to pass through it.<br /> <br /> Still another option is to use Correspondence 3. There is an interpretation of Correspondence - one that is not entirely unsupported by the books - that says that Correspondence 3 may be interpreted as allowing one to travel without the intervening space being an obstacle. Order of Reason characters in the Sorcerer's Crusade are capable of using Correspondence 3 and seemingly mundane tools to gain entry to a building much faster than normal. One might be able to use it to claim that walls are not an obstacle to the person's path, and walk right through them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T09:31:07-07:00","id":996117,"title":"","content":"I actually remember a rote in the...uh, perhaps 2nd Ed corebook that used *Prime* of all things to make the Mage essentially ethereal, with everything passing through them. However, it also meant being immobile and stuck in place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T14:06:02-07:00","id":996253,"title":"","content":"I remember of a 2nd rote with rubbing the bones (Prime 2 in M20 Prime 3) in conjunction with Mind to get the moment of least materiality and step througj the wall.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}